   "text": "Price-time is the equities standard AND the one the data structure expresses natively - the FIFO queue at each price level IS\ntime priority. Pro-rata would require walking every order at a level and computing allocations: O(orders at level), not O(1).\n\nThe honest observation: price-time CREATES the latency arms race that makes this entire design necessary. If matching were a\nperiodic batch auction, tens-of-microseconds latency would be pointless and the whole one-box architecture unjustified. The\ndesign's most extreme constraint is downstream of a market-design decision - which is a good thing to be able to see.",
   "originalText": "Price-time is the equities standard AND the one the data structure expresses natively - the FIFO queue at each price level IS\ntime priority. Pro-rata would require walking every order at a level and computing allocations: O(orders at level), not O(1).\n\nThe honest observation: price-time CREATES the latency arms race that makes this entire design necessary. If matching were a\nperiodic batch auction, tens-of-microseconds latency would be pointless and the whole one-box architecture unjustified. The\ndesign's most extreme constraint is downstream of a market-design decision - which is a good thing to be able to see.",
